{
  "title": "Selecting rows and columns",
  "summary": "Columns by name, rows by label with loc, by position with iloc, and by condition.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "loc and iloc",
      "body": [
        "Columns: `df[\"qty\"]` (a Series) or `df[[\"qty\", \"price\"]]` (a DataFrame).",
        "",
        "Rows (and both at once) go through two indexers:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "df.loc[row_label, col_label]     # by LABEL",
        "df.iloc[row_pos, col_pos]        # by POSITION (0-based, like lists)",
        "",
        "df.loc[1003, \"qty\"]              # the qty of the row labelled 1003",
        "df.iloc[0]                       # first row, whatever its label",
        "df.iloc[:, -1]                   # last column",
        "df.loc[1002:1004, [\"product\", \"qty\"]]",
        "```",
        "",
        "A **label slice includes its end** (`1002:1004` gives three rows); a position slice does",
        "not (`iloc[0:2]` gives two). With the default `0, 1, 2...` index, labels and positions look",
        "alike, until you sort or filter and they stop matching."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"qty\": [3, 1, 5, 2]}, index=[10, 20, 30, 40])",
        "print(len(df.loc[10:30]), len(df.iloc[0:2]))",
        "print(int(df.loc[20, \"qty\"]), int(df.iloc[-1, 0]))",
        "print(df.iloc[1:3].index.tolist())"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "3 2",
        "1 2",
        "[20, 30]"
      ],
      "explain": "`loc[10:30]` includes 30 (3 rows); `iloc[0:2]` stops before position 2 (2 rows)."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "After `df = df.sort_values(\"qty\")`, which always gives the row with the smallest `qty`?",
      "options": [
        "`df.iloc[0]`",
        "`df.loc[0]`",
        "`df[0]`",
        "`df.loc[\"qty\"].min()`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Sorting reorders rows but keeps their labels. `iloc[0]` is the first *position*; `loc[0]` is whichever row has the *label* 0. `df[0]` looks for a column named 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Filtering with conditions",
      "body": [
        "A boolean Series selects rows, exactly like a NumPy mask:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "df[df[\"qty\"] > 2]",
        "df[(df[\"region\"] == \"North\") & (df[\"qty\"] >= 3)]",
        "df[df[\"product\"].isin([\"Widget\", \"Gizmo\"])]",
        "df[df[\"price\"].between(5, 10)]          # inclusive both ends",
        "df.loc[df[\"qty\"] > 2, \"product\"]        # filter rows AND pick a column",
        "```",
        "",
        "`df.loc[mask, columns]` is the most useful form: filter and select in one step (and, as",
        "lesson 6 shows, the right way to *change* the selected cells)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Products sold in the North or East with a price above 5.",
      "code": [
        "import io",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(\"product,region,price\\nA,North,2\\nB,East,9\\nC,South,8\\nD,North,6\\n\"))",
        "mask = df[\"region\"].__1__([\"North\", \"East\"]) __2__ (df[\"price\"] > 5)",
        "print(df.__3__[mask, \"product\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "isin",
        "&",
        "loc"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "in",
        "and",
        "iloc",
        "|",
        "between"
      ],
      "explain": "Prints `['B', 'D']`."
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Label-based or position-based?",
      "buckets": [
        "By label",
        "By position"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "`df.loc[\"x\"]`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`df.iloc[0]`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`df.loc[:, \"price\"]`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`df.iloc[:, -1]`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`df.at[5, \"qty\"]`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`df.iat[2, 1]`",
          1
        ]
      ],
      "explain": "`at` and `iat` are fast single-cell versions of `loc` and `iloc`."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Expensive products",
      "prompt": [
        "`df` has columns `product`, `region`, `qty`, `price`. Write `expensive(df, min_price)` that",
        "returns a plain list of the **distinct** product names with `price >= min_price`, in the",
        "order they first appear. The tests use this `df`:",
        "",
        "| order_id | product | region | qty | price |",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|",
        "| 1001 | Widget | North | 3 | 2.50 |",
        "| 1002 | Gadget | South | 1 | 10.00 |",
        "| 1003 | Widget | South | 5 | 2.50 |",
        "| 1004 | Gizmo | East | 2 | 7.25 |",
        "| 1005 | Gadget | North | 4 | 10.00 |",
        "| 1006 | Gizmo | North | 1 | 7.25 |",
        "",
        "```python",
        "expensive(df, 7)   # [\"Gadget\", \"Gizmo\"]",
        "```",
        "",
        "Hint: `.unique()` keeps first-appearance order."
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef expensive(df, min_price):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def expensive(df, min_price):",
        "    return df.loc[df[\"price\"] >= min_price, \"product\"].unique().tolist()"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`df.loc[df[\"price\"] >= min_price, \"product\"]`",
        "Add `.unique().tolist()`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import io",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.read_csv(io.StringIO('order_id,product,region,qty,price\\n1001,Widget,North,3,2.50\\n1002,Gadget,South,1,10.00\\n1003,Widget,South,5,2.50\\n1004,Gizmo,East,2,7.25\\n1005,Gadget,North,4,10.00\\n1006,Gizmo,North,1,7.25\\n'))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"min_price 7\", [\"Gadget\", \"Gizmo\"], list(expensive(_df, 7)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"min_price 10 (inclusive)\", [\"Gadget\"], list(expensive(_df, 10)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"everything\", [\"Widget\", \"Gadget\", \"Gizmo\"], list(expensive(_df, 0)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"nothing\", [], list(expensive(_df, 100)))"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Orders in a range",
      "prompt": [
        "`df` is indexed by `order_id` (sorted ascending) with columns `product`, `region`, `qty`,",
        "`price`. Write `orders_between(df, first, last, region)` returning a plain list of the order",
        "ids from `first` to `last` **inclusive** that were in `region`. The tests use the orders from the",
        "previous step, with `order_id` as the index:",
        "",
        "| order_id | product | region | qty | price |",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|",
        "| 1001 | Widget | North | 3 | 2.50 |",
        "| 1002 | Gadget | South | 1 | 10.00 |",
        "| 1003 | Widget | South | 5 | 2.50 |",
        "| 1004 | Gizmo | East | 2 | 7.25 |",
        "| 1005 | Gadget | North | 4 | 10.00 |",
        "| 1006 | Gizmo | North | 1 | 7.25 |",
        "",
        "```python",
        "orders_between(df, 1002, 1005, \"North\")   # [1005]",
        "orders_between(df, 1001, 1006, \"North\")   # [1001, 1005, 1006]",
        "```",
        "",
        "Slice the rows by label with `loc`, then filter."
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef orders_between(df, first, last, region):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def orders_between(df, first, last, region):",
        "    part = df.loc[first:last]",
        "    return part[part[\"region\"] == region].index.tolist()"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`part = df.loc[first:last]` includes `last`.",
        "`part[part[\"region\"] == region].index.tolist()`"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import io",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.read_csv(io.StringIO('order_id,product,region,qty,price\\n1001,Widget,North,3,2.50\\n1002,Gadget,South,1,10.00\\n1003,Widget,South,5,2.50\\n1004,Gizmo,East,2,7.25\\n1005,Gadget,North,4,10.00\\n1006,Gizmo,North,1,7.25\\n'), index_col=\"order_id\")",
        "Dojo.eq(\"1002..1005 North\", [1005], list(orders_between(_df, 1002, 1005, \"North\")))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"all North\", [1001, 1005, 1006], list(orders_between(_df, 1001, 1006, \"North\")))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"both ends included\", [1002, 1003], list(orders_between(_df, 1002, 1003, \"South\")))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"none\", [], list(orders_between(_df, 1001, 1003, \"East\")))"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "iloc",
          "message": "Uses labels (loc), not positions"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
